    {
      "id": "g05-04",
      "title": "Express likes and dislikes",
      "sourcePages": "135",
      "meaning": "好き and きらい describe feelings about a thing or person. 大好き and 大きらい express stronger feelings.",
      "formation": "Person は thing が 好き / きらい です. Treat these words as な-adjectives; before a noun use 好きな / きらいな.",
      "notes": [
        "The liked thing normally takes が, not を. Use は when explicitly contrasting it with another thing.",
        "A milder dislike can be expressed as あまり好きじゃないです.",
        "私の好きな本 means a book I like; の marks the person here. Neutral 好きでもきらいでもないです means neither like nor dislike.",
        "Use the noun version of an activity here; verb + の is introduced in Lesson 8."
      ],
      "prerequisites": [
        "g05-01",
        "g05-03"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "english": "Nao really likes tea.",
          "japanese": "奈緒さんはお茶が大好きです。",
          "kana": "なおさんはおちゃがだいすきです。"
        },
        {
          "english": "I do not like fish very much.",
          "japanese": "私は魚があまり好きじゃないです。",
          "kana": "わたしはさかながあまりすきじゃないです。"
        }
      ],
